WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.890
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:06.210
Today I want to talk about progress
videos, how they can be an important

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.980
part of your language learning strategy.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.799
Remember if you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe click

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.440
on the bell for notifications.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:18.450
If you're listening to this on a
podcast, uh, please leave a review.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.010
Okay.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.810
So what do I mean by progress videos?

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.510
Uh, I'm about to do one by the way.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.710
It's, uh, I think four or five minutes
of me speaking, in fact I have done it.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.460
It's four or five minutes of me
speaking in Persian, in Farsi,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:38.550
uh, you know that I'm on a 90-Day
Challenge, half Arabic, half Persian.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.790
I want to improve my
level in these languages.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.600
So I've done a video
where I speak in Persian.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.680
I speak about my experience
of learning Persian, what I've

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.210
been doing to learn Persian.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.310
What has helped me to learn Persian.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.170
So this then becomes a record of
where I am on that date, roughly at

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.750
the midpoint of my 90-Day Challenge.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.210
I'm going to put this up on YouTube.

00:01:03.269 --> 00:01:03.960
People will look it.

00:01:04.815 --> 00:01:08.865
As is usually the case some
people will say, that's very nice.

00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:10.515
Some people will criticize.

00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:12.765
Some people will say you just read it.

00:01:12.945 --> 00:01:16.994
And a whole range of reactions, most
of the reactions are very encouraging,

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:18.735
which is the way it should be.

00:01:19.095 --> 00:01:24.975
But the big thing about a progress video
is you, it's a, it's an opportunity for

00:01:24.975 --> 00:01:29.985
you to sort of take a snapshot of where
you are at a particular point in time.

00:01:30.554 --> 00:01:35.940
And I've often felt that, um, maybe
even at LingQ we should have, like

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.809
everyone should have a portfolio where
they can have things they have written.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.759
Obviously we have the statistics of
how many words you've learned and

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:50.970
LingQs you've saved and stuff, but
also regular milestones of each learner

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.270
speaking in the language they're
learning: two minutes, one minute,

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.429
three minutes, five minutes, either a
monologue or speaking with someone else.

00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:05.175
And so over time, this then becomes a
record of who you are in that language.

00:02:05.744 --> 00:02:12.225
Um, to some extent my, uh, tutor
reports are a record because I

00:02:12.225 --> 00:02:14.295
can go back six months, 12 months.

00:02:14.295 --> 00:02:15.435
I can do that in Arabic.

00:02:15.765 --> 00:02:19.695
I can do it in Persian now, or
going back to Turkish or any other

00:02:19.695 --> 00:02:20.954
language where I've had a tutor.

00:02:20.954 --> 00:02:25.245
And I can look at my, uh,
tutor report, which the tutors

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.745
have usually recorded for me.

00:02:27.085 --> 00:02:31.065
And I can recollect again where I was
at that point in time in my learning.

00:02:31.815 --> 00:02:38.055
But uh, now creating this sort of,
um, video record of, of where I am my

00:02:38.055 --> 00:02:42.105
progress, uh, I think it's very valuable
and it has a number of advantages.

00:02:42.105 --> 00:02:45.735
First of all, in order to produce a
three or five minute video speaking,

00:02:46.215 --> 00:02:48.315
uh, it forces you to concentrate.

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:51.765
And then obviously you're going to
look at what you said, and you're

00:02:51.765 --> 00:02:54.675
going to discover, you're going
to see without anyone pointing

00:02:54.675 --> 00:02:55.925
them out, all the mistakes.

00:02:56.715 --> 00:03:01.005
So it is a very good way of becoming
aware of where your shortcomings are,

00:03:01.005 --> 00:03:02.715
so that you can then work on them.

00:03:03.255 --> 00:03:07.454
Uh, you'll get comments from other
people which may also be important.

00:03:07.454 --> 00:03:07.995
But I think...

00:03:08.345 --> 00:03:13.845
the main thing is that you get to focus
in on where you are in the language.

00:03:14.325 --> 00:03:16.665
And so I would like to encourage
other people to do this.

00:03:18.465 --> 00:03:22.305
But talk specifically, talk about
what you have been doing in the

00:03:22.305 --> 00:03:26.475
language, what has worked for you,
but do it in your target language.

00:03:26.685 --> 00:03:30.765
And I'd be quite happy to look
at these, uh, comment on them.

00:03:30.765 --> 00:03:31.065
I've...

00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:36.105
depending on how many we get, I may
not be able to comment on all of them.

00:03:36.495 --> 00:03:41.220
Uh, obviously I'm particularly interested
in people who are using LingQ, uh,

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:45.959
to learn a language and to hear from
them in their language, uh, what their

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.600
experience has been, sorry, in their...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:51.120
in the language they are learning, to
hear what their experience has been.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:56.970
Um, yeah, I think, and, and of course, uh,
just as I put this on YouTube, which is

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:03.899
a, a form of social media and I will tweet
it out, uh, people may want to, uh, post

00:04:03.899 --> 00:04:09.840
these progress videos on their various,
you know, social media outlets because,

00:04:10.515 --> 00:04:14.655
well, we learned for ourselves language
learning is such a rewarding thing to do.

00:04:14.655 --> 00:04:16.965
It's something that we also
want to share with other people.

00:04:17.415 --> 00:04:23.895
So again, I'd be interested in people's
reactions to this idea of regular progress

00:04:23.895 --> 00:04:31.005
videos, uh, as, uh, all of us in our own
way, uh, are engaged in this a rewarding

00:04:31.005 --> 00:04:33.735
journey of learning other languages now.

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:40.140
So I will leave you with my progress
video, uh, in Persian and I look forward

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:44.670
to seeing you, uh, uh, come back to
me with where you have done progress

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.500
videos and where they can be found.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.060
So thank you for listening.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.060
And, uh, I look forward to seeing
those progress videos, and now here's

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.290
some Persian and don't be too hard
on me because this is unrehearsed

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.300
and I'm just letting it all hang out.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.020
Okay.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:58.290
Bye.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:58.500
For now.

